The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (IS_GEN9_LP(dev_priv) || IS_CANNONLAKE(dev_priv)) {
    signal_levels = bxt_signal_levels(intel_dp);
}
```
Reason:
The conditional check incorrectly includes only generation 9 and Cannon Lake devices, which means that devices of generation 10 and above (like Ice Lake) are not accounted for, leading to the use of incorrect signal levels.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (IS_GEN9_LP(dev_priv) || INTEL_GEN(dev_priv) >= 10) {
    signal_levels = bxt_signal_levels(intel_dp);
}
```
Reason:
The patch updates the conditional check to include devices of generation 10 and above by replacing `IS_CANNONLAKE(dev_priv)` with `INTEL_GEN(dev_priv) >= 10`, ensuring that the correct signal levels are used for ICL architecture.

